Offline pages: the module ships the English tldr-pages (read-only) in /system/etc/android-linux-tools/share/tldr
with the layout of tealdeer's cache (pages.en/<platform>/<page>.md). When the user cache has no pages.* directory
(nothing downloaded yet, or an `--update` that failed after creating the directory), page lookups and --list
use the shipped pages; --update, auto-update and --clear-cache work on the user cache only, as before. No cache
age warning for the shipped pages (their mtime is the build's SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH).
Source: android-linux-tools (no upstream or distribution equivalent: Termux packages/tealdeer and aports
testing/tealdeer ship no pages and download them with `tldr --update`); cache layout from tealdeer's
src/cache.rs (Cache::find_page, Language::directory_name).
